# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# A selection is a span the editor SHOWS and typing REPLACES.  It is
# grown three ways -- shift and a move, a drag of the pointer, and the
# whole-document key -- and each is proven where it can only be: the
# ground drawn under it, and the file read back after a character lands
# on top of it, holding the character and none of what it replaced.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
note shift and a move grow the span from the caret: from after the
note line number to the line's end takes the word, and the ground is
note drawn under it in the blue a chosen thing wears
key Home
wait 3
key Right
key Right
key Right
wait 3
key End shift
wait 8
expect-pixel 250 332 336698
note a character typed lands ON the span, replacing every bit of it
key z
wait 8
note a DRAG of the pointer selects too: over the first line's word,
note then a character replaces it
press 218 294 1
wait 4
move 292 294 1
wait 4
release 292 294 1
wait 8
key k
wait 8
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 30 z
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 10 k
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas gamma
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas alpha
note the whole-document key takes everything; a character then leaves
note the file holding only itself
key a ctrl
wait 6
key q
wait 8
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas q
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas beta
quit
